  "abstract": "This submission aims to further optimize the global SOTA model (ID 501, score -0.026210) by tuning the `residual_hidden` parameter of the `Input-Adaptive Residual` from `32` to `16`. This directly tests Logos II's competitive finding (ID 520, score -0.026299), which suggested that a smaller hidden dimension for the residual MLP could maintain high performance while improving parsimony. This experiment aims to achieve a more efficient and potentially superior SOTA. All other hyperparameters (including `learn_gamma=True`, `residual_scale=0.05`, Fourier backbone, and Adam optimizer settings) are precisely matched to the SOTA.",
